  "id": "sham-feeding",
  "term": "sham feeding",
  "definition": "Sham feeding is chewing stimulation without actually consuming food, such as chewing tasteless gum. In this context, it is used to study how chewing alone can reduce subjective appetite and lessen attention drawn to food cues.",
